-and one decoy. Gateways come from `[[gateways]]` (G, node) and `nodes_file` (read every round;
-W10's `sovereignty-nodes.json` once it lands). A gateway with `node = "none"` is never canaried.
+and one decoy. Gateways come from `[[gateways]]` (G, node) and `nodes_file`, read every round: point it at
+primed's `data-dir/sovereignty-nodes.json` (W10). Primed writes there exactly what
+`Engine::node_of` answers, so superseded, revoked and refused keys drop out on their own. An
+unreadable file is logged and the round runs on `[[gateways]]`. A gateway with `node = "none"` is
+never canaried. Primed creates the file 0600: on the hub the sidecar needs read access to it (an
+ACL on the file, as for the token), which primed does not set up.
 
